==Marketing==
First images and poster art were released on October 26, 2020, during Netflix's Anime Festival, with the streaming service releasing a teaser trailer later that same day.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cbr.com/netflix-godzilla-singular-point-trailer-poster-images/|title=Netflix's Godzilla Singular Point Anime Debuts First Trailer, Poster and Images|date=October 26, 2020|first=Collier |last=Jennings|website=[[Comic Book Resources]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201027122647/https://www.cbr.com/netflix-godzilla-singular-point-trailer-poster-images/|archive-date=October 27, 2020|url-status=live|access-date=October 27, 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://screenrant.com/godzilla-singular-point-anime-show-new-images-poster/|title=Godzilla: Singular Point Images Reveal New Look At Anime Show|date=October 26, 2020|first=Daniel |last=Alvarez|website=[[Screen Rant]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201027122905/https://screenrant.com/godzilla-singular-point-anime-show-new-images-poster/|archive-date=October 27, 2020|url-status=live|access-date=October 27, 2020}}</ref> The teaser revealed that the series would air in April 2021 and would feature monsters and characters from the [[Godzilla (franchise)#Shōwa era (1954–1975)|Shōwa era]] of the [[Godzilla (franchise)|''Godzilla'' franchise]], such as [[Rodan]], [[Anguirus]], [[Jet Jaguar]], [[Manda (kaiju)|Manda]], and what initially appeared to be [[Titanosaurus (Godzilla)|Titanosaurus]] and [[All Monsters Attack|Gabara]]<ref>{{cite web|url=https://screenrant.com/godzilla-singular-point-show-trailer-netflix/|title=Godzilla: Singular Point Trailer Reveals New Animated Forms of Classic Monsters|date=October 27, 2020|first=Daniel |last=Alvarez|website=[[Screen Rant]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201028131913/https://screenrant.com/godzilla-singular-point-show-trailer-netflix/|archive-date=October 28, 2020|url-status=live|access-date=October 28, 2020}} url=</ref>—the latter two later being revealed as new kaiju Godzilla Aquatilis and Salunga. On October 12, 2020, it was announced that Takahashi, EnJoe, Bones producer Naoki Amano, Orange producer Jiro Ando, and [[Toho]] producer Takashi Yoshizawa would all appear in a panel during the ''Godzilla Fest Online 2020'' event on November 3, 2020.<ref>{{cite tweet|user=GODZILLA_SP|number=1315550558334271488|date=October 12, 2020|title=11月3日(火祝)の配信イベント「ゴジラ・フェス オンライン2020」(https://godzilla.store/gfes/2020online)内にて、『#ゴジラSP』トークステージ配信が決定しました。出演：高橋敦史(監督)/円城塔(シリーズ構成・脚本)/天野直樹(ボンズプロデューサー)/安藤次郎(オレンジプロデューサー)/吉澤隆(東宝プロデューサー)|trans-title="#Godzilla SP" talk stage distribution has been decided in the distribution event "Godzilla Festival Online 2020" (https://godzilla.store/gfes/2020online) on November 3 (Tuesday). Cast: Atsushi Takahashi (Director) / Toh Enjoe (Series Composition / Screenplay) / Naoki Amano (Bonds Producer) / Jiro Ando (Orange Producer) / Takashi Yoshizawa (Toho Producer)|language=ja|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201029010438/https://twitter.com/GODZILLA_SP/status/1315550558334271488|archive-date=October 29, 2020|url-status=live|access-date=October 28, 2020}}</ref> On February 12, 2021, the full design of Godzilla was revealed, illustrated by Eiji Yamamori and colored by Yūji Kaneko.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/daily-briefs/2021-02-13/godzilla-singular-point-anime-reveals-title-monster-design/.169466|title=Godzilla Singular Point Anime Reveals Title Monster's Design|first=Adriana |last=Hazra|website=[[Anime News Network]]|date=February 13, 2021|access-date=February 13, 2021}}</ref>

''Godzilla Singular Point'' received a DVD/Blu-ray release in Japan in three separate volumes: the first volume was released on August 18, 2021, with the other two on September 22 and October 20.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://tokusatsunetwork.com/2021/05/godzilla-singular-point-comes-to-dvd-blu-ray-in-japan/|title=Godzilla: Singular Point Comes to DVD & Blu-Ray in Japan|first=Rex|last=Xeno|website=Tokusatsu Network|date=May 27, 2021|access-date=May 27, 2021}}</ref> The show also received [[Bandai]] soft vinyl action figures as part of the ''Movie Monster'' series toyline. The first to be revealed was of Jet Jaguar and Godzilla in his Ultima form on March 6, 2021, in Japan.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.scifijapan.com/merchandise/godzilla-singular-point-figures-from-bandai|title=GODZILLA SINGULAR POINT Figures From Bandai|website=SciFi Japan|date=March 6, 2021}}</ref> These two were later followed up by another vinyl figure of Godzilla in his Aquatilis form on April 17.<ref name="Bandai">{{cite web|url=https://www.scifijapan.com/godzilla-toho/new-godzilla-singular-point-figures-from-bandai|title=New GODZILLA SINGULAR POINT Figures From Bandai|website=SciFi Japan|date=April 17, 2021}}</ref> Vinyl figures of Angurius and Manda were released on April 24.<ref name="Bandai"/> A vinyl figure of Godzilla in his Amphibia form to follow on May 15,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.scifijapan.com/godzilla-toho/godzilla-singular-point-godzilla-amphibia-figure-from-bandai|title=GODZILLA SINGULAR POINT Godzilla Amphibia Figure From Bandai|website=SciFi Japan|date=May 15, 2021}}</ref> and his Terrestris form one week later on May 22.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.scifijapan.com/godzilla-toho/bandai-releases-godzilla-singular-point-godzilla-terrestris-figure|title=Bandai Releases GODZILLA SINGULAR POINT Godzilla Terrestris Figure|website=SciFi Japan|date=May 22, 2021}}</ref>

